.TH SANCHALA-CLEANER 1 "August 2026" "Sanchala OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sanchala-cleaner \- System maintenance and cleanup tool for Sanchala OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sanchala-cleaner
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sanchala-cleaner
performs system maintenance tasks including package cache cleanup,
temporary file removal, log rotation, and orphan package removal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B analyze
Analyze disk usage and cleanup opportunities
.TP
.B clean \fR[\fICATEGORY\fR]
Perform cleanup (all, cache, logs, tmp, orphans)
.TP
.B schedule \fR[\fBenable\fR|\fBdisable\fR|\fBstatus\fR]
Manage automatic cleanup schedule
.TP
.B rules
List active cleanup rules
.TP
.B dry-run
Show what would be cleaned without removing
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-aggressive
More thorough cleanup (may remove useful caches)
.TP
.B \-\-keep-days \fIN\fR
Keep files newer than N days (default: 7)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Analyze cleanup opportunities:
.B sanchala-cleaner analyze
.TP
Clean package cache:
.B sanchala-cleaner clean cache
.TP
Full cleanup with confirmation:
.B sanchala-cleaner clean all
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sanchala/cleaner/cleaner.toml
Configuration file
.TP
.I /etc/sanchala/cleaner/rules.d/
Cleanup rule definitions
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paccache (8),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR tmpfiles.d (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Sanchala OS Team <dev@sanchala.id>
